    {
      "id": 110415,
      "name": "Craig",
      "username": "Craig",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/craig/{size}/2150_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-28T18:50:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Maybe I should try Cosmic Encounter, again. The first time I played (years ago) I was so turned off by the fact I couldn't even pick who I was attacking, I had a horrible experience. I've since learned it's a social game, not a tactical one, so maybe I can accept it on those terms…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, it's a social game to the nth degree. It's also incredibly cutthroat in its social-ness, to the point that there are people I just cannot play it with. Not for the thin-skinned. Not so much as Diplomacy, though…</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
