    {
      "id": 110416,
      "name": "Silverleaf",
      "username": "Silverleaf",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-07-28T20:05:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Maybe I should try Cosmic Encounter, again. The first time I played (years ago) I was so turned off by the fact I couldn't even pick who I was attacking, I had a horrible experience. I've since learned it's a social game, not a tactical one, so maybe I can accept it on those terms…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I've played twice, and hated it both times. It seemed to boil down to trying to persuade people to help you for a while, a comparison of pretty random numbers on cards, and an exchange that basically goes, \"I win!\" \"No you don't!\" \"Yes I do!\" \"Aha! Now&nbsp;<em>nobody</em> wins!\" It's like Munchkin but without the vaguely amusing card names and illustrations.&nbsp;</p>",
